# Requests and Review (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/requests.md`, `docs/modules/review.md`, ADR-022)

Two linked features. Module names are `support_requests*` (not `requests`, which would shadow the HTTP library).

## Requests invariants
- Thread subjects = `subject_id` + linked questions' `subject_id` copies. **Visible:** reporter, admins of any of them, super admins (general thread: reporter + super). **Manage:** admin of any. **Approve:** admin of **every** one (super for general). Use `access_for` / `visible_filter`; never hand-roll a check in a route.
- Status rules live in the pure `allowed_statuses` / `status_after_reply` / `needs_agent`. The agent may never set `approved`; only `decide_approval` does. Reject needs a note → status `open`.
- `status_after_reply`: any person's reply (role `reporter` **or** `manager`; a reporter who is also an admin is `manager`) to `needs_info` / `resolved` → `open`; `closed` stays closed. Never key a rule on `role == 'reporter'` alone.
- `last_actor_kind` drives the agent queue: a person's message / status change / decision sets it; `add_system_note` never does.
- Agent wake webhook (ADR-023, `app/agent_wake.py`): every route where a person changes a thread reads `was_needed = srs.needs_agent(...)` before the change and calls `agent_wake.notify(req, was_needed)` **after** its commit. Never before the commit, never from agent tools. Payload = ids / status / title only (no message text, attachments, tokens); log the host only (the URL path may be a credential). Best effort: never let it fail the person's action. URL / secret are `.env` only.
- Attachments: written only by `save_attachments` under `storage.request_dir(id)` via `safe_join`, served only by `/requests/attachment/<id>` after the visibility check; images inline, everything else `application/octet-stream` download, `nosniff`. Never serve the folder statically.
- Message bodies are plain text rendered by `render_body` (escape first). Do not add markup without escaping.
- Live thread: the page and `GET /requests/<id>/live` render the same `partials/request_thread_body.html`; the poll swaps `#rqHeader` / `#rqThread` / `#rqReplyNotice` / `#rqStatusBox` / `#rqBatches` by id (keep them; fields inside need ids to survive). `support_requests.thread_live` stays in `web_security.PASSIVE_ENDPOINTS` or open tabs defeat the idle limit. Images are `a.rq-zoom` (delegated preview modal), never `target="_blank"`.
- Subject delete: `detach_subject` (threads become general); user erase nulls reporter / author / closed_by.
- `REQUESTS_ENABLED` off → `/requests/*` 404 and Report buttons hidden (`requests_can_report()`, `window.OQB_REPORT_URL`).

## Review invariants
- Items are `[{field, old, new}]` over `question_edit_service.FIELDS` (taxonomy as ids). Apply only through `review_service.apply_item` → `qes.apply_fields(action='review-apply')`; Apply all takes one point and passes `capture=False`.
- Stale (`old` ≠ current) → 409 until `confirm_stale`; Apply all leaves stale items pending.
- `log_corrections` runs **after** the commit and never raises.
- Every batch / item route: `@admin_required` + `authz.require_subject(batch.subject_id, 'admin')`.

## Gotchas
- `question_edit_service` is shared by the Edit modal (`update_question` → `write_values`), Review and the agent (`apply_fields`): a rule change affects all three; run `tests.test_question_edit_service`, `tests.test_review_service`.
- Stems cannot hold tags, level, type or marks (`FIELDS[f]['leaf']`; `normalize_changes(stem=True)` refuses).
- Every UI string through `t()` / `OQB.t()` with a `zh_Hant.json` key; `STATUS_LABELS`, `CATEGORY_LABELS` and `FIELDS` labels are covered by `test_dynamic_keys_are_translated`.
- Composer posts `FormData` by `fetch` (CSRF header from `csrf.js`); plain forms need `{{ csrf_field() }}`. `showToast` is not global outside the Edit modal partial.
